From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 20:59:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: remove the Zed (cloud) edit-prediction provider option
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Drop EditPredictionProvider::Zed — the only provider that routes edit
prediction through Zed's hosted/authenticated endpoints. Edit prediction
now requires a user-provided self-hosted model (Ollama / OpenAI-compatible
private server) or a BYO-key provider (Mercury, Codestral). Stale
"provider": "zed" settings migrate to None via fallible-options.

Removes the variant + its account UI (sign-in/usage/data-collection arms
gated on the Zed provider) from settings_content, the registry mapping,
agent_ui, and the status-bar button. The store's cloud machinery is
removed separately in the next patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
